Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** that flips when you hover over it.  
It uses only HTML & CSS (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  color: #fff;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
}

/* Styling for front side */
.card .front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Styling for back side */
.card .back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #43cea2, #185a9d);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* Start flipped */
}

/* Hover effect: flip the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front content -->
    <div class="front">
      <span>Front Side</span>
    </div>
    <!-- Back content -->
    <div class="back">
      <span>Back Side</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the 3D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides and applies the rotation animation. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each side of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that should not be visible. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Positions the back side behind the front initially. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the whole card 180° around the Y‑axis when hovered. |

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside the `<span>` tags, adjust colors, or change dimensions to fit your design. Enjoy!
